# Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides. Both are optional.

# Where the Next server proxies /api/* (see `rewrites` in next.config.ts).
# Default: http://localhost:8000
#
# Read per-request by the Next server, NOT inlined into the browser bundle, so
# changing it needs only a restart. Set it when the API is somewhere other than
# localhost — a container on another port, or a machine on your LAN.
#API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# Absolute base URL for the backend, which BYPASSES the proxy above and makes
# the browser call the API directly. Leave unset for local development and
# tunnel testing; the same-origin proxy avoids CORS entirely.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, so this needs a rebuild to change —
# which is exactly why it is not used for tunnels, whose hostnames change per
# session. Set it only for a deployment with a stable API domain.
#
# Must be https:// for any deployed build: a page served over https cannot
# fetch an http:// API (mixed content), and the failure is silent apart from a
# console error.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
